<p>Note that the copyright in a photograph inserted in a literary or academic work and created specifically for that work lasts for the same term as the copyright in that work (Art. 24 of the Copyright Act of 1899).
</p>
<div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Old_motion_pictures" data-mw-thread-id="h-Old_motion_pictures-Terms"><span data-mw-comment-start="" id="h-Old_motion_pictures-Terms"></span>Old motion pictures<span data-mw-comment-end="h-Old_motion_pictures-Terms"></span></h3></div>
<p>The following tables apply to cinematographic works <b>made public on or before December 31, 1970</b>, and to images derived from such works. Cinematographic works made public after that date generally remain protected, with quite rare exceptions that had been unpublished for more than 50 years before publication.
</p><p>For works that identify individual authors (typically directors) in the published work:
</p>
<table class="wikitable" style="width:100%">
<tbody><tr>
<th>Death date of<br>the last surviving author</th>
<th>Date of publication</th>
<th style="width:55%;">Copyright tag
</th></tr>
<tr>
<th rowspan="3">– 31 December 1957
</th>
<th>– 31 December 1930
</th>
<td style="background-color: #F0F8FF;"><a href="/wiki/Template:PD-Japan-film" title="Template:PD-Japan-film"><span style="font-family:monospace,monospace;">{{PD-Japan-film}}</span></a><br><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r360851041"><span class="monospaced">{{<a href="/wiki/Template:PD-old-auto-expired" title="Template:PD-old-auto-expired">PD-old-auto-expired</a>|deathyear=<i>death year</i>}}</span>
</td></tr>
<tr>
<th>1 January 1931 – <br>31 December 1945
</th>
