<div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Exceptions" data-mw-thread-id="h-Exceptions-Terms"><span data-mw-comment-start="" id="h-Exceptions-Terms"></span>Exceptions<span data-mw-comment-end="h-Exceptions-Terms"></span></h3></div>
<ul><li>For some government works, <a href="/wiki/Template:PD-Japan-exempt" title="Template:PD-Japan-exempt"><span style="font-family:monospace,monospace;">{{PD-Japan-exempt}}</span></a></li>
<li>Photographs of a <i>copyrighted</i> architectural work (architect or building designer not yet dead for more than 70 years) <a href="/wiki/Template:FoP-Japan" title="Template:FoP-Japan"><span style="font-family:monospace,monospace;">{{FoP-Japan}}</span></a> + <a href="/wiki/Commons:Choosing_a_license" title="Commons:Choosing a license">free license tag</a> for the image</li>
<li>Photographs of a <i>copyrighted</i> artwork or sculpture located in a public space (sculptor, painter, craftsman, or artisan not yet dead for more than 70 years) <a href="/wiki/Template:NoFoP-Japan" title="Template:NoFoP-Japan"><span style="font-family:monospace,monospace;">{{NoFoP-Japan}}</span></a> (Not accepted on Commons)<sup id="cite_ref-6" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-6"><span class="cite-bracket">[</span>6<span class="cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup></li>
<li>TOO (Logo) <a href="/wiki/Template:TOO-Japan" title="Template:TOO-Japan"><span style="font-family:monospace,monospace;">{{TOO-Japan}}</span></a> + <a href="/wiki/Commons:Licensing#Material_in_the_public_domain" title="Commons:Licensing">Public domain</a> for the image</li></ul>
<div class="mw-heading mw-heading2 ext-discussiontools-init-section"><h2 id="Copyright_tags" data-mw-thread-id="h-Copyright_tags"><span data-mw-comment-start="" id="h-Copyright_tags"></span>Copyright tags<span data-mw-comment-end="h-Copyright_tags"></span></h2></div>
<p><span id="TAG"></span>
</p>
<div class="shortcut2" style="background:var(--background-color-neutral-subtle, #f8f9fa); color:var(--color-base, #202122);" role="note"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r927745239"><a href="/wiki/Commons:Shortcuts" title="Commons:Shortcuts">Shortcut</a><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r574572692"><div class="plainlist">
<ul><li><span class="plainlinks"><a class="external text" data-mw-original-href="//commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Commons:TAG_Japan&amp;redirect=no" href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Commons:TAG_Japan&amp;redirect=no">COM:TAG Japan</a></span></li></ul>
</div></div>
<p><span dir="ltr">See also: <a href="/wiki/Commons:Copyright_tags" title="Commons:Copyright tags">Commons:Copyright tags</a></span>
</p>
<ul><li><a href="/wiki/Template:PD-Japan" title="Template:PD-Japan"><span style="font-family:monospace,monospace;">{{PD-Japan}}</span></a> – for Japanese non-photographic works 50 years after the death of the creator (there being multiple creators, the creator who dies last), or 50 years after publication for anonymous or pseudonymous authors. Valid for works whose author died before 1968.</li>
<li><a href="/wiki/Template:PD-Japan-oldphoto" title="Template:PD-Japan-oldphoto"><span style="font-family:monospace,monospace;">{{PD-Japan-oldphoto}}</span></a> – for Japanese photos published before 1 January 1958, or photographed before 1 January 1948.</li>
<li><a href="/wiki/Template:PD-Japan-film" title="Template:PD-Japan-film"><span style="font-family:monospace,monospace;">{{PD-Japan-film}}</span></a> – for motion pictures first published in Japan more than 70 years ago, in which no individual author is identified, or whose identified individual author(s) died more than 38 years ago.</li>
<li><a href="/wiki/Template:PD-Japan-organization" title="Template:PD-Japan-organization"><span style="font-family:monospace,monospace;">{{PD-Japan-organization}}</span></a> – for images of the works in names of organizations/companies/corporations 50 years after the publication. Valid for works by the name of organizations which were published before 1968.</li>
<li><a href="/wiki/Template:PD-Japan-exempt" title="Template:PD-Japan-exempt"><span style="font-family:monospace,monospace;">{{PD-Japan-exempt}}</span></a> – for works exempt from copyright in Japan.</li>
<li><a href="/wiki/Template:GJSTU1" title="Template:GJSTU1"><span style="font-family:monospace,monospace;">{{GJSTU1}}</span></a> - For contents made available on government websites under the Government of Japan Standard Terms of Use (Version 1.0).</li>
<li><a href="/wiki/Template:GJSTU-2.0" title="Template:GJSTU-2.0"><span style="font-family:monospace,monospace;">{{GJSTU-2.0}}</span></a> - For contents made available on government websites under the Government of Japan Standard Terms of Use (Ver.2.0); compatible with <a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">CC BY 4.0</a>. Note that the content on the site under GJSTU 2.0 is not automatically compatible with Commons.</li>
<li><a href="/wiki/Template:PDL1.0" title="Template:PDL1.0"><span style="font-family:monospace,monospace;">{{PDL1.0}}</span></a> - For contents made available on government websites under the Public Data License (Ver.1.0); compatible with <a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">CC BY 4.0</a>. Note that the content on the site under PDL1.0 is not automatically compatible with Commons.</li></ul>
<p>Non-copyright tags:
</p>
<ul><li><a href="/wiki/Template:FoP-Japan" title="Template:FoP-Japan"><span style="font-family:monospace,monospace;">{{FoP-Japan}}</span></a> may be added to a picture that includes architectural works, which are allowed under the "freedom of panorama" rule, but other tags should be given to show the picture's copyright status in Japan and the United States.</li>
<li><a href="/wiki/Template:AerialPhotograph-mlitJP" title="Template:AerialPhotograph-mlitJP"><span style="font-family:monospace,monospace;">{{AerialPhotograph-mlitJP}}</span></a> – The copyright holder, the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure, Transport and Tourism of Japan, allows anyone to use the image for any purpose, provided that the copyright holder is properly attributed.</li></ul>
<div class="mw-heading mw-heading2 ext-discussiontools-init-section"><h2 id="Currency" data-mw-thread-id="h-Currency"><span data-mw-comment-start="" id="h-Currency"></span>Currency<span data-mw-comment-end="h-Currency"></span></h2></div>
<p><span id="CUR"></span>
</p>
<div class="shortcut2" style="background:var(--background-color-neutral-subtle, #f8f9fa); color:var(--color-base, #202122);" role="note"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r927745239"><a href="/wiki/Commons:Shortcuts" title="Commons:Shortcuts">Shortcut</a><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r574572692"><div class="plainlist">
<ul><li><span class="plainlinks"><a class="external text" data-mw-original-href="//commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Commons:CUR_Japan&amp;redirect=no" href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Commons:CUR_Japan&amp;redirect=no">COM:CUR Japan</a></span></li></ul>
</div></div>
<p><span dir="ltr">See also: <a href="/wiki/Commons:Currency" title="Commons:Currency">Commons:Currency</a></span>
</p><p><span typeof="mw:File"><span><img src="https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/OOjs_UI_icon_check-constructive.svg/20px-OOjs_UI_icon_check-constructive.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="20" height="20" class="mw-file-element" srcset="https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/OOjs_UI_icon_check-constructive.svg/40px-OOjs_UI_icon_check-constructive.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="20" data-file-height="20"></span></span> <b><bdi>OK</bdi></b>. The designs of the Japanese banknotes are published as state-issued 'Notifications' which exempt them from copyright protection under Copyright Law of Japan.<sup id="cite_ref-MinFin1994_7-0" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-MinFin1994-7"><span class="cite-bracket">[</span>7<span class="cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup>
<a href="/wiki/Template:PD-Japan-exempt" title="Template:PD-Japan-exempt"><span style="font-family:monospace,monospace;">{{PD-Japan-exempt}}</span></a> applies to them.
<sup id="cite_ref-MinFin76-1984_8-0" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-MinFin76-1984-8"><span class="cite-bracket">[</span>8<span class="cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup>
</p>
<div class="mw-heading mw-heading2 ext-discussiontools-init-section"><h2 id="De_minimis" data-mw-thread-id="h-De_minimis"><span data-mw-comment-start="" id="h-De_minimis"></span>De minimis<span data-mw-comment-end="h-De_minimis"></span></h2></div>
<p><span id="DM"></span>
</p>
<div class="shortcut2" style="background:var(--background-color-neutral-subtle, #f8f9fa); color:var(--color-base, #202122);" role="note"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r927745239"><a href="/wiki/Commons:Shortcuts" title="Commons:Shortcuts">Shortcut</a><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r574572692"><div class="plainlist">
<ul><li><span class="plainlinks"><a class="external text" data-mw-original-href="//commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Commons:DM_Japan&amp;redirect=no" href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Commons:DM_Japan&amp;redirect=no">COM:DM Japan</a></span></li></ul>
</div></div>
<p><span dir="ltr">See also: <a href="/wiki/Commons:De_minimis" title="Commons:De minimis">Commons:De minimis</a></span>
</p><p>According to the <i>Copyright Act (Act No. 48 of May 6, 1970, amended up to January 1, 2022/April 1, 2026)</i>:
</p>
<ul><li>In the process of taking photographs, recording sounds or visuals, broadcasting, or otherwise reproducing images or sounds of objects or communicating them without undertaking reproduction (hereinafter in this paragraph, referred to as "act of reproducing or communicating"), any other work comprising objects or sounds that are captured incidentally along with the objects or sounds captured during the act of reproducing or communicating (hereinafter in this paragraph referred to as "objects or sounds captured for reproduction or communication") (those captured incidentally include the objects or sounds captured as constituting a part of the objects or sounds captured for reproduction or communication; hereinafter in this paragraph referred to as "incidentally captured objects or sounds") (but only another work that constitutes a minor part of the materials created or communicated by the act of reproducing or communicating (hereinafter in this Article referred to as "created or communicated materials"), in light of the percentage of the work in the created or communicated materials, the accuracy of its replication in the created or communicated materials, and other elements; hereinafter in this Article referred to as an "incidentally captured work") may be exploited, in any way, in connection with the act of reproducing or communicating, within the scope that is justified in light of the existence or nonexistence of the intention of making profit through the exploitation of the incidentally captured work, the degree of difficulty in separating the incidentally captured objects or sounds from the objects or sounds captured for reproduction or communication, the role to be played by the incidentally captured work in the created or communicated materials, and other elements; provided, however, that this does not apply if the action would unreasonably prejudice the interests of the copyright owner in light of the nature or purpose of the incidentally captured work or the circumstances of its exploitation.<span style="color:gray;font-size:80%;"><sup>[48/1970-2022-2026 Art. 30-2(1)]</sup></span></li>
<li>An incidentally captured work exploited pursuant to the provisions of the preceding paragraph may be exploited, in any way, in connection with the exploitation of the created or communicated materials relevant to the incidentally captured work; provided, however, that this does not apply if the action would unreasonably prejudice the interests of the copyright owner in light of the nature or purpose of the incidentally captured work or the circumstances of its exploitation.<span style="color:gray;font-size:80%;"><sup>[48/1970-2022-2026 Art. 30-2(2)]</sup></span></li></ul>
<dl><dt>Note</dt>
<dd>"Addition by Act No. 43 of 2012; Partial Amendment of Act No. 30 of 2018 and Act No. 48 of 2020"</dd></dl>
<div class="mw-heading mw-heading2 ext-discussiontools-init-section"><h2 id="Freedom_of_panorama" data-mw-thread-id="h-Freedom_of_panorama"><span data-mw-comment-start="" id="h-Freedom_of_panorama"></span>Freedom of panorama<span data-mw-comment-end="h-Freedom_of_panorama"></span></h2></div>
<p><span id="FOP"></span>
</p>
<div class="shortcut2" style="background:var(--background-color-neutral-subtle, #f8f9fa); color:var(--color-base, #202122);" role="note"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r927745239"><a href="/wiki/Commons:Shortcuts" title="Commons:Shortcuts">Shortcut</a><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r574572692"><div class="plainlist">
<ul><li><span class="plainlinks"><a class="external text" data-mw-original-href="//commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Commons:FOP_Japan&amp;redirect=no" href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Commons:FOP_Japan&amp;redirect=no">COM:FOP Japan</a></span></li></ul>
</div></div>
<p><span dir="ltr">See also: <a href="/wiki/Commons:Freedom_of_panorama" title="Commons:Freedom of panorama">Commons:Freedom of panorama</a></span>
</p>
<ul><li>for artistic works: <span typeof="mw:File"><span><img src="https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/OOjs_UI_icon_close-ltr-destructive.svg/20px-OOjs_UI_icon_close-ltr-destructive.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="20" height="20" class="mw-file-element" srcset="https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/OOjs_UI_icon_close-ltr-destructive.svg/40px-OOjs_UI_icon_close-ltr-destructive.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="20" data-file-height="20"></span></span>&nbsp;<b>Not OK</b> {{<a href="/wiki/Template:NoFoP-Japan" title="Template:NoFoP-Japan">NoFoP-Japan</a>}} except in cases governed by Article 46.</li>
<li>for buildings only: <span typeof="mw:File"><span><img src="https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/OOjs_UI_icon_check-constructive.svg/20px-OOjs_UI_icon_check-constructive.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="20" height="20" class="mw-file-element" srcset="https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/OOjs_UI_icon_check-constructive.svg/40px-OOjs_UI_icon_check-constructive.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="20" data-file-height="20"></span></span> <b>OK</b> {{<a href="/wiki/Template:FoP-Japan" title="Template:FoP-Japan">FoP-Japan</a>}}</li></ul>
<p>According to the <i>Copyright Act (Act No. 48 of May 6, 1970, amended up to January 1, 2022/April 1, 2026)</i>:
</p>
<ul><li>It is permissible to exploit an artistic work the original copy of which is permanently installed in an outdoor location as provided for in paragraph (2) of the preceding Article or an architectural work, in any way whatsoever except the following:</li></ul>
<dl><dd><dl><dd>(i) producing additional copies of a sculpture or making those additional copies of the sculpture available to the public by transferring them;</dd>
<dd>(ii) reproducing an architectural work by means of construction, or making copies of an architectural work so reproduced available to the public by transferring them;</dd>
<dd>(iii) reproducing a work in order to permanently install it in an outdoor location as provided for in paragraph (2) of the preceding Article;</dd>
<dd>(iv) reproducing an artistic work for the purpose of selling copies of it, or selling those copies.<span style="color:gray;font-size:80%;"><sup>[48/1970-2022-2026 Art. 46]</sup></span></dd></dl></dd></dl>
<p>The outdoor locations sppecified in the preceding article are "on a street, at a park, or in any other outdoor location accessible to the public, or on the outer wall of a building or other place easily seen by the public."<span style="color:gray;font-size:80%;"><sup>[48/1970-2022-2026 Art. 45(2)]</sup></span>
</p><p>Architectural works located in such places, including buildings, gardens, bridges and towers (<a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="https://monolith.law/en/general-corporate/building-image-use-illegal">source</a>), may be photographed and the photos may be reproduced for any purposes. The restriction on "selling" copies only applies to the "artistic works." However, non-commercial licenses <a href="/wiki/Commons:Licensing" title="Commons:Licensing">are not free enough for Commons</a>. Some buildings like the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/en:Tower_of_the_Sun" class="extiw" title="w:en:Tower of the Sun">Tower of the Sun</a> can be regarded as artistic works per <a href="/wiki/Commons_talk:Freedom_of_panorama/Archive_1#Hideyuki_Murata" title="Commons talk:Freedom of panorama/Archive 1">discussion</a>.
</p><p>Regarding buildings, a <a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="http://www.courts.go.jp/app/files/hanrei_jp/737/010737_hanrei.pdf">2003 ruling by the Osaka District Court</a> states that in order for a building to be copyrighted, it "must have creativity in aesthetic expression in light of the definition of works stipulated in Article 2, Paragraph 1, Item 1 of the same Act." This means ordinary-looking buildings are not eligible for copyright protection as "architectural works".
</p><p>For more information, refer to:
</p>
<ul><li><a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="http://www.murata-law.jp/kigyou/cs-kenchiku.html">著作権法 – 建築に関する著作物について (Copyright Law – About Architectural Works)</a>, by 村田法律事務所 (Murata Law Office) (<a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20090901103724/http://www.murata-law.jp/kigyou/cs-kenchiku.html">archived copy</a>) — in Japanese</li></ul>
<dl><dt>Mandatory attribution even in derivative works, except in the case of anonymous works</dt></dl>
<ul><li>In a case set forth in one of the following items, the source of the work must be clearly indicated in the manner and to the extent considered reasonable, commensurate with the circumstances of its reproduction or exploitation:... a work is exploited other than by its reproduction pursuant to the provisions of Article 32 or Article 42, or is exploited pursuant to the provisions of Article 35, paragraph (1); Article 36, paragraph (1); Article 38, paragraph (1); Article 41; Article 41-2, paragraph (2); Article 42-2, paragraph (2); <b>Article 46</b>; or Article 47-5, paragraph (1), and it is common practice to indicate the source.<span style="color:gray;font-size:80%;"><sup>[48/1970-2026 Art. 48(1)(iii)]</sup></span></li>
<li>In a source indication as referred to in the preceding paragraph, the name of the author that appears on the work must be cited, except if the author's name is clear from the source indication or if the work is anonymous.<span style="color:gray;font-size:80%;"><sup>[48/1970-2026 Art. 48(2)]</sup></span></li>
<li>If a work is exploited as provided in one of the following items, the source of the original work underlying the derivative work provided for in that item must be indicated pursuant to the provisions of the preceding two paragraphs:... a derivative work created pursuant to the provisions of Article 40, paragraph (1); <b>Article 46</b>; or Article 47-5, paragraph (1) is exploited pursuant to those provisions.<span style="color:gray;font-size:80%;"><sup>[48/1970-2026 Art. 48(3)(i)]</sup></span></li></ul>
<dl><dt>Notes</dt>
<dd></dd></dl>
<ul><li><i>Article 46:</i> "Partial Amendment of Act No. 77 of 1999." <i>Article 48:</i> "Partial Amendment of Act No. 62 of 1985; Act No. 56 of 2000; Act No. 85 of 2003; Act No. 121 of 2006; Act No. 53 of 2009; Act No. 30 of 2018; Act No. 39 of 2018; and Act No. 33 of 2023)."</li>
<li>According to the copyright law, Japan has a copyright duration of 70 years after the death of the author (ie. creator/designer) or following "the death of the last surviving co-author in the case of a joint work." Henceforth, the author's works shall become copyright free and enter the public domain.<span style="color:gray;font-size:80%;"><sup>[48/1970-2022-2026 Art. 51]</sup></span></li></ul>
<style data-mw-deduplicate="TemplateStyles:r916284754">.mw-parser-output .see-also{background:var(--background-color-interactive-subtle,#f8f9fa);margin:1em 0;border:1px solid var(--border-color-subtle,#c8ccd1);padding:2px;color:var(--color-base,#202122);clear:left;overflow:hidden}</style><div role="note" class="see-also"><span class="mw-valign-middle" typeof="mw:File"><span><img src="https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/System-search.svg/40px-System-search.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="25" height="25" class="mw-file-element" srcset="https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/System-search.svg/60px-System-search.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="48" data-file-height="48"></span></span>See also: <a href="/wiki/Category:Japanese_FOP_cases" title="Category:Japanese FOP cases">Category:Japanese FOP cases</a>. </div>
<p><br>
</p>
<div class="mw-heading mw-heading2 ext-discussiontools-init-section"><h2 id="Stamps" data-mw-thread-id="h-Stamps"><span data-mw-comment-start="" id="h-Stamps"></span>Stamps<span data-mw-comment-end="h-Stamps"></span></h2></div>
<p><span dir="ltr">See also: <a href="/wiki/Commons:Stamps" title="Commons:Stamps">Commons:Stamps</a></span>
</p><p><span typeof="mw:File"><span title="Copyrighted"><img alt="Copyrighted" src="https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Red_copyright.svg/40px-Red_copyright.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="25" height="25" class="mw-file-element" srcset="https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Red_copyright.svg/60px-Red_copyright.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="197" data-file-height="197"></span></span> Generally speaking, stamps are considered as organizational works ("work-for-hire"). Stamps issued before 1946 are acceptable for Commons; otherwise, not acceptable due to URAA restoration or regular 70-year copyright protection. Note that there could be exceptions, e.g., a derivative work of individual works.
</p>
<div class="mw-heading mw-heading2 ext-discussiontools-init-section"><h2 id="Threshold_of_originality" data-mw-thread-id="h-Threshold_of_originality"><span data-mw-comment-start="" id="h-Threshold_of_originality"></span>Threshold of originality<span data-mw-comment-end="h-Threshold_of_originality"></span></h2></div>
<p><span id="TOO"></span>
</p>
<div class="shortcut2" style="background:var(--background-color-neutral-subtle, #f8f9fa); color:var(--color-base, #202122);" role="note"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r927745239"><a href="/wiki/Commons:Shortcuts" title="Commons:Shortcuts">Shortcut</a><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r574572692"><div class="plainlist">
<ul><li><span class="plainlinks"><a class="external text" data-mw-original-href="//commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Commons:TOO_Japan&amp;redirect=no" href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Commons:TOO_Japan&amp;redirect=no">COM:TOO Japan</a></span></li></ul>
</div></div>
<p><span dir="ltr">See also: <a href="/wiki/Commons:Threshold_of_originality" title="Commons:Threshold of originality">Commons:Threshold of originality</a></span>
</p><p>Logos in the gallery below are <span typeof="mw:File"><span><img src="https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/OOjs_UI_icon_check-constructive.svg/20px-OOjs_UI_icon_check-constructive.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="20" height="20" class="mw-file-element" srcset="https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/OOjs_UI_icon_check-constructive.svg/40px-OOjs_UI_icon_check-constructive.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="20" data-file-height="20"></span></span> <b>OK</b> to upload. 
Article 2 of Japanese copyright law defines that a work is eligible for copyright when it is a production in which thoughts or sentiments are expressed in a creative way and which falls within the literary, scientific, artistic or musical domain.<sup id="cite_ref-Law1980_9-0" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-Law1980-9"><span class="cite-bracket">[</span>9<span class="cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup>
</p><p>Japanese courts have decided that to be copyrightable, a text logo needs to have artistic appearance that is worth artistic appreciation. Logos composed merely of geometric shapes and texts are also not copyrightable in general. 
</p>
<table class="wikitable">
<tbody><tr>
<td><span typeof="mw:File"><a href="/wiki/File:Asahi_logo.svg" class="mw-file-description" title="Asahi Breweries &quot;Asahi&quot; logo"><img alt="Asahi Breweries &quot;Asahi&quot; logo" src="https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Asahi_logo.svg/250px-Asahi_logo.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="150" height="58" class="mw-file-element" srcset="https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Asahi_logo.svg/330px-Asahi_logo.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="950" data-file-height="370"></a></span>
</td>
<td>(<a href="/wiki/Commons:Deletion_requests/File:Asahi_logo.svg" title="Commons:Deletion requests/File:Asahi logo.svg">DR</a>) Tokyo High Court's ruling: letters are a means of communication, shared by all. Copyright protection of fonts is limited only to those that raise artistic appreciation as much as artistic works do.<sup id="cite_ref-Tokyo1470_10-0" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-Tokyo1470-10"><span class="cite-bracket">[</span>10<span class="cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup>
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td><span typeof="mw:File"><a href="/wiki/File:Cup_Noodles.jpg" class="mw-file-description" title="Cup Noodles"><img alt="Cup Noodles" src="https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Cup_Noodles.jpg/250px-Cup_Noodles.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="150" height="100" class="mw-file-element" srcset="https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Cup_Noodles.jpg/330px-Cup_Noodles.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="1936" data-file-height="1296"></a></span>
</td>
<td>(<a href="/wiki/Commons:Deletion_requests/File:Cup_Noodles.jpg" title="Commons:Deletion requests/File:Cup Noodles.jpg">DR</a>) Tokyo High Court's ruling: although the shape is stylized, the text is in a normal arrangement and keeps its function of being read as a sequence of letters.<sup id="cite_ref-Tokyo14233_11-0" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-Tokyo14233-11"><span class="cite-bracket">[</span>11<span class="cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup>
</td></tr>
<tr>
<td><span typeof="mw:File"><a href="/wiki/File:Olympic_flag.svg" class="mw-file-description" title="Olympic flag"><img alt="Olympic flag" src="https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Olympic_flag.svg/250px-Olympic_flag.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="150" height="100" class="mw-file-element" srcset="https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Olympic_flag.svg/330px-Olympic_flag.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="900" data-file-height="600"></a></span>
</td>
<td>Tokyo District Court's ruling: the Court is negative towards recognizing the symbol as a copyrightable work of fine arts, because it is considered merely relatively simple graphic elements.<sup id="cite_ref-Tokyo5594_12-0" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-Tokyo5594-12"><span class="cite-bracket">[</span>12<span class="cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup>
</td></tr></tbody></table>
<ul><li>In Japan, the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Furby" class="extiw" title="w:Furby">Furby</a> toy is <a href="/wiki/Commons:Derivative_works#UTILITY" title="Commons:Derivative works">utilitarian</a> and hence not protected by copyright as an artistic work. Photos of the toy cannot be uploaded to Commons as it is not utilitarian in the United States.<sup id="cite_ref-Sendai2009_13-0" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-Sendai2009-13"><span class="cite-bracket">[</span>13<span class="cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup></li></ul>
<div class="mw-heading mw-heading2 ext-discussiontools-init-section"><h2 id="Signatures" data-mw-thread-id="h-Signatures"><span data-mw-comment-start="" id="h-Signatures"></span>Signatures<span data-mw-comment-end="h-Signatures"></span></h2></div>
<p><span id="SIG"></span>
</p>
<div class="shortcut2" style="background:var(--background-color-neutral-subtle, #f8f9fa); color:var(--color-base, #202122);" role="note"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r927745239"><a href="/wiki/Commons:Shortcuts" title="Commons:Shortcuts">Shortcut</a><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r574572692"><div class="plainlist">
<ul><li><span class="plainlinks"><a class="external text" data-mw-original-href="//commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Commons:SIG_Japan&amp;redirect=no" href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Commons:SIG_Japan&amp;redirect=no">COM:SIG Japan</a></span></li></ul>
</div></div>
<p><span dir="ltr">See also: <a href="/wiki/Commons:When_to_use_the_PD-signature_tag" title="Commons:When to use the PD-signature tag">Commons:When to use the PD-signature tag</a></span>
</p><p><span typeof="mw:File"><span><img src="https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/OOjs_UI_icon_check-constructive.svg/20px-OOjs_UI_icon_check-constructive.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="20" height="20" class="mw-file-element" srcset="https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/OOjs_UI_icon_check-constructive.svg/40px-OOjs_UI_icon_check-constructive.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="20" data-file-height="20"></span></span> <b><bdi>OK</bdi></b> for a typical signature, <span typeof="mw:File"><span><img src="https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/OOjs_UI_icon_close-ltr-destructive.svg/20px-OOjs_UI_icon_close-ltr-destructive.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="20" height="20" class="mw-file-element" srcset="https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/OOjs_UI_icon_close-ltr-destructive.svg/40px-OOjs_UI_icon_close-ltr-destructive.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="20" data-file-height="20"></span></span>&nbsp;<b>Not OK</b> for calligraphic signatures. The decision <a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="https://www.courts.go.jp/app/hanrei_jp/detail7?id=54774">平成10(受)332</a> (Hanrei Jiho No. 1730: 123) set a relatively high artistic threshold for typefaces. The decision <a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="https://www.courts.go.jp/app/hanrei_jp/detail7?id=13555">平成10(ワ)14675</a> substantiates that calligraphy works are copyrightable <sup id="cite_ref-14" class="reference"><a href="#cite_note-14"><span class="cite-bracket">[</span>14<span class="cite-bracket">]</span></a></sup>.  According to  Article 2, Paragraph 1, Item 1 of the Copyright Law, a <i>work is a production in which thoughts or sentiments are expressed in a creative way and which falls within the literary, scientific artistic or musical domain</i>. A signature must have <i>aesthetic properties capable of artistic appreciation</i>, not just <i>beauty in terms of practical functionality</i>, to be copyrightable.
</p>
<div class="mw-heading mw-heading2 ext-discussiontools-init-section"><h2 id="See_also" data-mw-thread-id="h-See_also"><span data-mw-comment-start="" id="h-See_also"></span>See also<span data-mw-comment-end="h-See_also"></span></h2></div>
<ul><li><a href="/wiki/Japan" class="mw-redirect" title="Japan">Japan</a></li>
<li><a href="/wiki/Category:License_tags_of_Japan" title="Category:License tags of Japan">Category:License tags of Japan</a></li>
<li><a href="/wiki/Category:Stamps_of_Japan" title="Category:Stamps of Japan">Category:Stamps of Japan</a></li></ul>
<ul><li><a href="https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/ja:%E3%83%98%E3%83%AB%E3%83%97:%E3%83%91%E3%83%96%E3%83%AA%E3%83%83%E3%82%AF%E3%83%89%E3%83%A1%E3%82%A4%E3%83%B3" class="extiw" title="s:ja:ヘルプ:パブリックドメイン">s:ja:ヘルプ:パブリックドメイン</a> (Wikisource: Help: Public Domain)</li>
<li><a href="https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/ja:%E8%91%97%E4%BD%9C%E6%A8%A9%E6%B3%95_(%E6%98%8E%E6%B2%BB%E4%B8%89%E5%8D%81%E4%BA%8C%E5%B9%B4%E6%B3%95%E5%BE%8B%E7%AC%AC%E4%B8%89%E5%8D%81%E4%B9%9D%E5%8F%B7)" class="extiw" title="s:ja:著作権法 (明治三十二年法律第三十九号)">s:ja:著作権法 (明治三十二年法律第三十九号)</a> (Wikisource: Copyright Act 1899)</li>
<li><a href="https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/ja:%E8%91%97%E4%BD%9C%E6%A8%A9%E6%B3%95" class="extiw" title="s:ja:著作権法">s:ja:著作権法</a> (Wikisource: Copyright Act 1970)</li>
<li><a href="https://meta.wikimedia.org/wiki/Legal/URAA_Statement" class="extiw" title="m:Legal/URAA Statement">m:Legal/URAA Statement</a></li>
